<ReportItem port="443" svc_name="www" protocol="tcp" severity="4" pluginID="153584" pluginName="Apache 2.4.49 Path Traversal and Remote Code Execution (CVE-2021-41773)" pluginFamily="Web Servers">
<description>The version of Apache httpd installed on the remote host is 2.4.49. It is, therefore, affected by a path traversal vulnerability in the path normalization code (CVE-2021-41773). An unauthenticated, remote attacker can exploit this to read files outside the document root and, if CGI scripts are enabled, execute arbitrary code.</description>
<solution>Upgrade to Apache version 2.4.51 or later.</solution>
<synopsis>The remote web server is affected by a path traversal vulnerability.</synopsis>
<cvss3_base_score>9.8</cvss3_base_score>
<cvss3_vector>CVSS:3.0/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H</cvss3_vector>
